    "## Derivations for parameter sweep:\n",
    "Begin with full energy and angular momentum expressions (in COM frame)\n",
    "### $E = \\frac{1}{2}m_1v_1^2 + \\frac{1}{2}m_2v_2^2 - \\frac{Gm_1m_2}{|r_1 - r_2|}$\n",
    "### $L = m_1(r_1 \\times v_1) + m_2(r_2 \\times v_2)$\n",
    "\n",
    "also the COM frame implies:\n",
    "### $m_1 r_1 + m_2 r_2 = 0$\n",
    "### $m_1 v_1 + m_2 v_2 = 0$\n",
    "\n",
    "reduction to one body:\n",
    "### $r = r_1 - r_2$\n",
    "### $v = v_1 - v_2$\n",
    "### $M = m_1 + m_2$\n",
    "### $\\mu = \\frac{m_1 m_2}{m_1+m_2}$\n",
    "inserting which  into the COM conditions gives:\n",
    "### $r_1 = \\frac{m_2 r}{M}$, $r_2 = -\\frac{m_1 r}{M}$\n",
    "### $v_1 = \\frac{m_2 v}{M}$, $v_2 = -\\frac{m_1 v}{M}$\n",
    "insert these into E and L expressions to obtain an equivalent one-body problem with mass $\\mu$:\n",
    "### $E = \\frac{1}{2}\\mu v^2 - \\frac{Gm_1 m_2}{r}$ \n",
    "### $L = \\mu (r \\times v)$\n",
    "now use Keplerian orbit formulation\n",
    "### $v^2 = \\dot{r}^2 + r^2\\dot{\\theta}^2$ \n",
    "### $L = \\mu r^2 \\dot{\\theta} => \\dot{\\theta} = \\frac{L}{\\mu r^2}$\n",
    "substitute $v^2$ into energy equation:\n",
    "### $E = \\frac{1}{2} \\mu \\dot{r}^2 + \\frac{L^2}{2\\mu r^2}-\\frac{Gm_1 m_2}{r}$\n",
    "at pericentre $\\dot{r} = 0$ =>\n",
    "\n",
    "# $E = \\frac{L^2}{2\\mu r_p^2}-\\frac{Gm_1 m_2}{r_p}$\n",
    "\n",
    "then substitute the orbit (conic section) equation\n",
    "### $r(f) = \\frac{p}{1+e \\ cos f}$, where f is true anomaly\n",
    "into the above energy equation to get the eccentricity:\n",
    "\n",
    "# $e = \\sqrt{1+\\frac{2EL^2}{\\mu^3 G^2 (m_1+m_2)^2}}$\n",
    "again from the conic section equation, setting r=r_p and inserting eccentricity we get:\n",
    "# $r_p = \\frac{L^2}{\\mu G m_1 m_2 (1+e)}$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "so, for the sweep we need:\n",
    "### $m_1, m_2, E, L$ => $e, r_p$\n",
    "\n",
    "to initialize initial conditions, we again use the relative seperation:\n",
    "### $r(f) = \\frac{p}{1+e \\ cos f}$, where f is true anomaly and p:\n",
    "### $p = \\frac{L^2}{\\mu G (m_1 + m_2)}$\n",
    "\n",
    "now, $r$ and $v$ vectors are expressed as:\n",
    "### $r = r(f) \\ [(cos f)_x \\ (sin f)_y]$\n",
    "### $v = \\frac{G(m_1 + m_2) \\mu}{L} \\ [(-sin f)_x \\ (e+cos f)_y]$\n",
    "\n",
    "and from the previous expressions we already have:\n",
    "### $r_1 = \\frac{m_2 r}{M}$, $r_2 = -\\frac{m_1 r}{M}$\n",
    "### $v_1 = \\frac{m_2 v}{M}$, $v_2 = -\\frac{m_1 v}{M}$\n",
    "\n",
    "to initialize one simulation we can choose an r value (that we keep the same for all cases)\n",
    "from the r value we find the true anomaly f and thus the initial r & v values!"
   ]
